# Final WebKit layout runner independent review

This follow-up preserves the preliminary `.tmp/review-webkit-baseline` evidence unchanged. The first source snapshot is in source/, the case/Break correction in marker-fix/, and the final no-wrap CSS and runner in nowrap-fix/. The last copies are byte-checked against commit 58f84716997b345dcda39746d3a6708a33b5ec41. No production edits by this reviewer.

The thirteen-case raw corpus is copied from `.tmp/doc13/corpus-after.log`, SHA d61bceddc2ac4ced366c91f01094efb6e9535be3309526547681e0ff396190b6. It records the actual Rust test `html::browser_layout_corpus_from_real_doc_source`, one passed/zero failed, with separate compile stderr. The producer was read directly: it calls the existing real Doc parse/lower/render helper on literal and explicit constructor inputs, including Break, nested reading/notes and two surrounding lines. This reviewer independently executed the browser runner on these exact outputs; did not independently rebuild the Rust producer for this follow-up.

All final 702 measurements passed: thirteen cases, two widths (375/1280), three font sizes (12/20/32), three line heights (normal/1.2/2), Chromium 151.0.7922.34, Firefox 153.0 and WebKit 26.5, Playwright 1.62.0 on Windows with document JavaScript disabled. The final complete output is nowrap-results.json. Earlier results.json/fixed-results.json represent earlier runner/CSS checkpoints, not the final no-wrap guarantee.

One independent WIP runner false-positive was reproduced and fixed: replacing Z by X in real line-reservation HTML skipped both surrounding-line measurements and accepted line_gaps=[]. The original mutated HTML, script and result are preserved. The final runner takes caseName and requires Z/Y once each plus two actual breaks, exact line-gap count, D/B in multiline cases and actual ordered multiline separation. Independently tested missing Z, missing Y, removed and hidden Break in each relevant case, and valid originals across all three engines: the 39 checks in mutation-results.json pass their respective failure/success expectations. The four managed Python tests also passed. A nonexistent explicit Chromium executable exited 1 with result=failed; missing/duplicate/nonhex/invalid-UTF8 corpus tests remain failures.

Root independently discovered caption implicit wrapping after the preliminary baseline review. The original alignment and overlap checks did not establish no-wrap behavior; that limitation is explicit rather than retroactively declaring the first fallback fully correct. The final fallback adds white-space:pre to its atomic containers, retaining explicit Break/newline and whitespace while suppressing implicit caption wrapping. This reviewer reproduced old-CSS long-reading fragmentation on WebKit and confirmed the final CSS rejects that regression through per-text-node fragment counts while preserving multiline originals. The first version of this diagnostic used an 80px paragraph: the whole valid atomic box moved to a new line, so comparing it with A on the previous line was an invalid expectation. mutations.initial.py is retained; the corrected 1280px control isolates internal caption wrapping. This helper correction is not a product failure.

The CSS remains a seven-line feature-query fallback. Supported engines keep inline-grid; unsupported baseline-source is recorded and accepted when behavior is correct. All reading/note/base nodes remain in source order; no JS, hidden text, RawHtml, offsets or transforms are introduced. The final no-wrap change refines the existing max-content requirement rather than reducing annotation content. Preliminary aria snapshots and line-height observations are retained as bounded prior evidence; actual assistive technology, printing, Safari on Apple platforms, forced colors and arbitrary user styles are not certified here.

CI checks the exact single Rust test name and uses `--exact --nocapture`; a zero-test or old seven-case log is rejected by the thirteen-case extractor. Browser binaries are installed for all three engines from the explicitly pinned requirements, including Playwright 1.62.0 and exact direct dependencies. No missing-engine skip/continue-on-error exists. doc-browser has a twenty-minute job timeout, and the always-run quality job requires its result to equal success. Evidence upload also runs on failure. CLI argument/corpus-read failures before result initialization exit unsuccessfully without a new result file; consumers must honor exit status and not interpret a preexisting output JSON as a fresh pass. CI's fresh output directory and required successful job avoid that false-success path.

Spec05/20 and development accurately distinguish unchanged typed span/semantic HTML from changed CSS layout and static browser tests from Wasm/Playground/assistive-technology acceptance. [CSS2 inline-block baseline](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS2/visudet.html#leading) and [table baseline rules](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS2/tables.html#height-layout) were consulted directly. Source order/accessibility and supported-feature observations remain as described in the earlier review. No remaining blocking issue reproduced in the final fixed scope. This does not approve canonical migration or Pages publication.
